This bumps sessions whose cursor IS the parent — i.e., sessions to which the new message is being appended (their path gains a node). The injecting session's cursor, at the time of the injected's persistence (inside the done flush), is the ASSISTANT node (just advanced by the assistant's persistence) → parentCursor === cursor → bump ✓ correct (the injecting session's path gains the injected message).

For a fork session with cursor at the assistant node: the injected message is NOT appended to the fork's path (the fork's cursor stays put; the injected is a child of the assistant on the main session's branch). But the bump logic would bump the fork too → wrong (off by one count).

