Hmm, but actually — is the main session's cursor X before the append? Yes. And the bump happens after persisting… The logic snapshots the sessions where cursor === parentCursor BEFORE advancing the cursor (that's the point of the earlier fix: "snapshot the snapshot's cursor-owning session IDs before advancing the cursor"). The appending session's cursor is X (=== parentCursor) → gets bumped ✓. The fork with cursor X also gets bumped ✗.

