session-status.cache.test.ts: The snapshot seed (buildSnapshotEvent) is used in test 1 to verify that repeated status reads don't mutate the event history (KV cache invariant). In v2, replace the snapshot seed with a merged `message` event + tool.result (the v2 persistence unit). Also, `buildContextMessagesFromEventHistory` is still a valid function (it exists in folding.js) — keep it. Remove the `SessionSnapshot` import, and rework buildSnapshotEvent into buildMessageEvents that returns an array of `message` + `tool.result` events.

Also — the comment block at the top mentions `cachedSystemPrompt/dynamicContextHash` as LLM-side caches — in v2, fold-types no longer has these… The invariant (that status projection never touches the LLM cache) is still valid (test 2 simulates these fields as local variables — no problem, no code changes needed; but FoldedSessionState no longer has these fields — the test just uses local consts, so it's still a valid "invariant" test… actually, test 2 is somewhat tautological now (stringify of local variables before and after — of course they don't change). It's a static invariant test, and test 3 (import check) is the substantive one. Keep test 2 as-is (harmless), and update the comment to remove references to fields that no longer exist? The comment says "must never touch the LLM-side caches: cachedSystemPrompt, cachedTools, dynamicContextHash, warmupState" — warmupState still exists (the warmup module), and cachedTools probably exists too. cachedSystemPrompt/dynamicContextHash were snapshot-era fields of FoldedSessionState. Keep the comment mostly as-is (warmup/cachedTools remain concepts of the LLM request path). Actually, to minimize risk, only change what's broken: the imports + snapshot seed.

