Note: For v1 payloads, the zod schema will fail first (events without eventId, missing cursorEventId) → parseSessionExport throws ZodError, so the version check will never be reached against v1. In other words, the "Unsupported session export version" error is unreachable against v1 documents (because the schema requires v2's shape). Hmm — this is an actual UX concern: users importing a v1 export will get an inscrutable Zod error instead of "v1 exports are no longer supported in v3+".

To give a clear error, check the version before the full schema parse: in parseSessionExport, first check the `format` marker and `version`, and throw a clear error for version 1. Let's update parseSessionExport:

```ts
export function parseSessionExport(payload: unknown): ParsedSessionExport {
  const candidate = payload as { format?: unknown; version?: unknown } | null
  if (candidate && candidate.format === SESSION_EXPORT_FORMAT && candidate.version === 1) {
    throw new Error('Session export version 1 (pre-v3) is not supported by this release — re-export the session from an OpenFox v2.9.x/v3.0-beta runtime')
  }
  return sessionExportSchema.parse(payload)
}
```

